---
import MarketingLayout from '../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';
import LegalShell from '../components/marketing/LegalShell.astro';
---

<MarketingLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="ATW.Net privacy policy: how we collect, use, and protect information across atw.net and ATW products."
  canonical="https://atw.net/privacy-policy"
>
  <LegalShell title="Privacy Policy" effective="November 3, 2026">
    <section class="rounded-xl border border-border p-6">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Introduction</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
        No Name Marketing, LLC, doing business as ATW.Net ("ATW," "we," "us," or "our"), operated from
        13940 Cedar Rd 438, University Heights OH 44118-3204, takes your privacy seriously. This Privacy Policy explains
        how we collect, use, disclose, and safeguard information when you visit
        <a href="https://atw.net" class="text-primary underline">atw.net</a> or use ATW products and services, including
        ATW One (ERP/CRM), WorkSuite, Hub, Mail, Auth (<a href="https://auth.atw.net" class="text-primary underline">auth.atw.net</a>),
        Pay, Directory, One AI, Agents/Workforce, and related communications by email, phone, and SMS/MMS.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
        By using our website or services, you acknowledge this policy. For product-specific messaging rules, see also our
        <a href="/sms-terms" class="text-primary underline">SMS Terms</a>,
        <a href="/cookies" class="text-primary underline">Cookie settings</a>, and
        <a href="/privacy-choices" class="text-primary underline">Your Privacy Choices</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="rounded-xl border border-border p-6">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Information we collect</h2>

      <h3 class="mt-6 text-lg font-medium">Personal information</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-muted-foreground">
        We may collect personal information that you voluntarily provide when you:
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-2 list-inside list-disc text-muted-foreground">
        <li>Register for an account or start a trial</li>
        <li>Sign up for a newsletter or product updates</li>
        <li>Contact us through our website, phone, email, or SMS</li>
        <li>Request a demo, consultation, or support</li>
        <li>Use ATW One, WorkSuite, Hub, Mail, Auth, Pay, Directory, One AI, Agents/Workforce, or related apps</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
        This information may include your name, email address, phone number, company name, billing details you submit,
        and any other information you choose to provide.
      </p>

      <h3 class="mt-6 text-lg font-medium">Automatically collected information</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-muted-foreground">
        When you visit our website or use our services, we automatically collect certain information about your device
        and usage, including:
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-2 list-inside list-disc text-muted-foreground">
        <li>IP address (see ATW Analytics below for how we store it)</li>
        <li>Browser type and operating system</li>
        <li>Pages or screens visited</li>
        <li>Time and date of visits</li>
        <li>Approximate location derived from network signals where needed for security or service operation</li>
      </ul>

      <h3 class="mt-6 text-lg font-medium">ATW Analytics</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-muted-foreground">
        We use ATW Analytics, our first-party analytics service, on atw.net and related pages. It loads a small
        JavaScript file that stores a pseudonymous visitor identifier in your browser localStorage and a session
        identifier in sessionStorage. These IDs are random UUIDs, not your name or email, until you submit a form that
        optionally links them to your contact information in our CRM.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-muted-foreground">
        ATW Analytics records page paths (including query strings where present), page titles, referrers, UTM campaign
        parameters, and custom events. Our servers also derive a truncated IP address (IPv4 /24 or IPv6 /48) and a salted
        hash of your IP address for abuse filtering and coarse geography. We do not accept IP addresses from the browser
        script. Raw analytics events are retained for about 90 days; daily summaries and journey data may be kept longer.
        When you submit a contact, trial, or lead form, we may store the analytics visitor and session IDs on your CRM
        record to understand how you found us.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-muted-foreground">
        We may also use third-party analytics or marketing tags (such as Google Analytics) as described in our
        <a href="/cookies" class="text-primary underline">Cookie settings</a>. You can control cookies through your browser
        settings and the choices described on our
        <a href="/privacy-choices" class="text-primary underline">Your Privacy Choices</a> page.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="rounded-xl border border-border p-6">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">How we use your information</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">We use the information we collect to:</p>
      <ul class="mt-2 list-inside list-disc text-muted-foreground">
        <li>Provide, maintain, and secure ATW products and services</li>
        <li>Create and administer accounts, including sign-in through Auth</li>
        <li>Improve our website, products, and user experience</li>
        <li>Communicate with you about services, support, billing, and account updates</li>
        <li>Send newsletters, product updates, and marketing communications you have opted into</li>
        <li>Respond to inquiries and support requests</li>
        <li>Monitor and analyze usage patterns and trends (including via ATW Analytics)</li>
        <li>Detect, prevent, and address fraud, abuse, or security incidents</li>
        <li>Comply with legal obligations</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="rounded-xl border border-border p-6">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">ATW Workforce and connected mailboxes</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
        <a href="https://workforce.atw.net/" class="text-primary underline">ATW Workforce</a> lets you connect a personal
        mailbox to a Workforce agent so the agent can send and manage email on your behalf when you allow those actions.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
        You may connect personal Gmail (and other providers when we offer them) with OAuth. For a Gmail connection, we
        request send, compose, and modify access for that user's mailbox only. We use the connection only to perform the
        agent email actions you allow in Workforce.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
        OAuth tokens for a connected mailbox are stored on ATW servers for that agent connection. We do not sell this data,
        and we do not use it for advertising.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
        You can disconnect a mailbox in Workforce. You can also revoke ATW's access in your Google Account connections (or
        the equivalent settings for other providers).
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
        Questions about Workforce mailbox connections:
        <a href="mailto:admin@atw.net" class="text-primary underline">admin@atw.net</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="rounded-xl border border-border p-6">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">SMS messaging and consent</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
        By providing your mobile phone number to ATW, you consent to receive SMS and/or MMS messages related to service
        notifications, account updates, project communications, support responses, and other information you have
        explicitly opted in to receive. Marketing SMS requires a separate, explicit opt-in where offered.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">Consent may be obtained through one or more of the following methods:</p>
      <ul class="mt-2 list-inside list-disc text-muted-foreground">
        <li>Verbal consent during a phone conversation</li>
        <li>Submission of a website or written form containing SMS disclosure</li>
        <li>Inbound SMS initiated by you</li>
        <li>Email or written authorization</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
        Message frequency may vary. Message and data rates may apply. You may opt out of SMS communications at any time by
        replying STOP. For assistance, reply HELP or contact us at
        <a href="mailto:support@atw.net" class="text-primary underline">support@atw.net</a>. Full messaging terms are in
        our <a href="/sms-terms" class="text-primary underline">SMS Terms</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="rounded-xl border border-border p-6">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Information sharing and disclosure</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
        We do not sell, trade, or rent your personal information to third parties.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">We may share your information with:</p>
      <ul class="mt-2 list-inside list-disc text-muted-foreground">
        <li>Service providers who assist in our operations (hosting, messaging, payment processing, support tooling)</li>
        <li>Law enforcement or regulators when required by law</li>
        <li>Professional advisors such as lawyers and accountants</li>
        <li>A successor entity in connection with a merger, acquisition, or asset sale, subject to this policy</li>
      </ul>

      <h3 class="mt-6 text-lg font-medium">SMS data protection</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-muted-foreground">
        No mobile information will be shared with third parties or affiliates for marketing or promotional purposes.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-muted-foreground">
        All other categories of personal information exclude text messaging originator opt-in data and consent; this
        information will not be shared with any third parties.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="rounded-xl border border-border p-6">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
        We use cookies and similar technologies to operate the site, remember preferences, support sign-in and security on
        product subdomains, and understand aggregate traffic. Details and controls are described in our
        <a href="/cookies" class="text-primary underline">Cookie settings</a> and
        <a href="/privacy-choices" class="text-primary underline">Your Privacy Choices</a> pages.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="rounded-xl border border-border p-6">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Security</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
        We implement appropriate technical and organizational security measures to protect your personal information from
        unauthorized access, disclosure, alteration, and destruction. However, no method of transmission over the Internet
        or electronic storage is 100% secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="rounded-xl border border-border p-6">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Your rights</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
        Depending on where you live (including California and other U.S. states with privacy laws), you may have the right
        to:
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-2 list-inside list-disc text-muted-foreground">
        <li>Access the personal information we hold about you</li>
        <li>Correct inaccurate information</li>
        <li>Request deletion of your information</li>
        <li>Opt out of marketing communications (email unsubscribe links; SMS STOP)</li>
        <li>Object to or limit certain processing where applicable</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
        To exercise these rights, email
        <a href="mailto:privacy@atw.net" class="text-primary underline">privacy@atw.net</a> or
        <a href="mailto:support@atw.net" class="text-primary underline">support@atw.net</a>, or use our
        <a href="/contact" class="text-primary underline">contact form</a>. Additional practical steps are on
        <a href="/privacy-choices" class="text-primary underline">Your Privacy Choices</a>. We may need to verify your identity
        before fulfilling a request.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="rounded-xl border border-border p-6">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Children</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
        Our website and services are directed to businesses and adults. We do not knowingly collect personal information
        from children under 13. If you believe a child has provided us personal information, contact
        <a href="mailto:privacy@atw.net" class="text-primary underline">privacy@atw.net</a> and we will take appropriate
        steps to delete it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="rounded-xl border border-border p-6">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Contact us</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
        Questions about this Privacy Policy or our practices:
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-2 list-inside list-disc text-muted-foreground">
        <li>
          Email:
          <a href="mailto:privacy@atw.net" class="text-primary underline">privacy@atw.net</a>
          or
          <a href="mailto:support@atw.net" class="text-primary underline">support@atw.net</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          Phone:
          <a href="tel:+13303332256" class="text-primary underline">+1 (330) 333-2256</a>
        </li>
        <li>Mail: No Name Marketing, LLC d/b/a ATW.Net, 13940 Cedar Rd 438, University Heights OH 44118-3204</li>
        <li>
          Web:
          <a href="/contact" class="text-primary underline">Contact form</a>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="rounded-xl border border-border p-6">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Updates to this policy</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
        We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The updated version will be indicated by an updated
        &ldquo;Last updated&rdquo; date at the top of this page and will be effective as soon as it is accessible. We
        encourage you to review this page periodically.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">Effective / last updated: November 3, 2026.</p>
    </section>
  </LegalShell>
</MarketingLayout>
